# Static CeTA with the help of docker and musl

Uses alpine-linux with musl in a docker container to build a fully statically linked executable,
*without any glibc nonsense*!

## Preparation

Place this directory in you CeTA root directory.

CeTA
├── docker-scripts    <--------- like this !!
│   ├── build-docker-static.sh
│   ├── build.sh
│   ├── Dockerfile
│   └── README
├── Makefile
├── src
...

in the `docker-scripts` directory run

    docker build -t alpine:ceta-build .

to create the docker image (once and for all)

## Usage

To build ceta run:

    ./docker-scripts/build-docker-static.sh

in the CeTA root directory.
